  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>NorthTec is a post-secondary higher education provider in Northland, New Zealand. The provider has several campuses across Northland in Auckland, Whangarei, Kaikohe, Kaitaia, Kerikeri, and Dargaville.</p><p>Since opening in 1978, the institution has grown to offer courses at foundation, certificate, diploma and degree levels. Students can now access around 100 courses in subjects like Business, Computing and IT, Nursing, Teaching, Engineering and more.</p><p>Education at NorthTec is challenging, varied, and exciting. You can choose from a wide range of courses, from nursing to construction.</p><p>NorthTecâ€™s Auckland International campus became the first centre in New Zealand to be approved by Immigration New Zealand for the Pearson Test of English Academic (PTE Academic)</p> <p>Across its several campuses, NorthTec has plenty of resources that students can access. The campus also has fitness and gym facilities at its health centre. Students can also socialise at The Apprentice Restaurant and student cafe and take in cultural events at the Geoff Wilson Art Gallery.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Students from various countries and continents attend NorthTec each year. Due to this, a diverse, welcoming and supportive culture is present across all campuses. International students can also receive help and guidance from highly qualified and trained staff.&nbsp;</p><p>The university also has an active Student Representation and Student Council. Students are encouraged to join these groups to become part of the institutionâ€™s community. In addition, these groups run and promote various student events throughout the year, which include welcome opportunities and off-campus trips.</p>"
